## Tooling

`pkgdx` (dev dependency) ships the Ruff, Mypy and PyMarkdown configs and their hooks.

- Lint, format, type-check and Markdown-lint with `uv run pkgdx-lint-hook`,
  `pkgdx-format-hook`, `pkgdx-typing-hook` and `pkgdx-markdown-hook`, not bare `ruff`, `mypy` or
  `pymarkdown`
- Do not add `[tool.ruff]`, `[tool.mypy]` or PyMarkdown config to `pyproject.toml`; line length
  is 79
- Exclude vendored or generated paths with `[tool.pkgdx] exclude` in `pyproject.toml`
- Do not hand-edit `pkgdx` entries in `prek.toml`, and do not run `uv run pkgdx init --reset`
  without first copying project hooks out of `prek.toml`
- See the [`pkgdx` reference](https://gitlab.com/andyrids/pkgdx/-/blob/main/docs/reference.md)
  for hooks, excludes, upgrades and config overrides

## Layout

- `src/{{import_package_name}}/` - Package source
- `tests/test_<module>.py` - Tests mirroring `src/`, with shared fixtures in `tests/conftest.py`
- `CHANGELOG.md` - Keep a Changelog

## Conventions

- Python >= {{python_min}}
- Implement only what is asked; prefer the standard library, then an existing dependency, and ask
  before adding one
{%- if cli %}

## CLI

The CLI in `src/{{import_package_name}}/__main__.py` is built on
[`pyclig`](https://github.com/andyrids/pyclig), which owns the CLI conventions.

- Do not reimplement exit codes, `-h`/`--help`, `-q`, `-d`/`--debug`, `--no-input`, colour or
  error output
- Send primary output to `ctx.out` (records via `ctx.emit`) and messages, logs and progress to
  `ctx.err`
- Use the `pyclig.options` helpers for common flags (`--json`, `--dry-run`, `--force`, `--output`)
- Test commands with `pyclig.testing.invoke`, and keep one `pyclig.testing.assert_conforms(cli)`
  test with a reason for each ignored rule
